	'ip_about_03' => 'Since 2014',
	'ip_about_04' => 'Our story in brief',
	'ip_about_05' => 'Founded in 2014 by clinical psychologist Mira Halden, Nodoka Counselling provides an unhurried, private space for psychotherapy in the Riverside District.',
	'ip_about_06' => 'A note from the founder',
	'ip_about_07' => 'I wanted a room where nobody|watches the clock.',
	'ip_about_08' => 'Where a sentence can stop halfway|and still be heard.',
	'ip_about_09' => 'Where you set the pace,|and we keep to it.',
	'ip_about_10' => 'Our founding and history',
	'ip_about_11' => 'Nodoka Counselling began in 2014 when Mira Halden opened our first consulting room in the Riverside District. Having spent years working within large healthcare institutions, Mira saw firsthand how administrative pressures and rigid time constraints often compromised therapeutic care. She wanted to build an independent practice centered on quiet attention, continuity, and genuine human regard. Over the subsequent years, our practice has grown thoughtfully into a collaborative team of six dedicated professionals. While our collective clinical expertise has broadened to support individuals and couples navigating a wide spectrum of life difficulties, our foundational commitment has never wavered: to offer a calm, protected room where people can speak candidly and be heard without haste.',
	'ip_about_12' => 'The values that guide our care',
	'ip_about_13' => 'Our practice is guided by three core values that inform every interaction. First, we practice unhurried listening, respecting each client\'s unique cadence rather than rushing toward premature conclusions. Second, we provide steady continuity, offering reliable weekly appointments that create emotional stability during times of upheaval or distress. Third, we work through collaborative inquiry. We do not view therapy as an expert delivering prescriptive advice to a passive recipient. Instead, practitioner and client sit together as equals, exploring patterns of thought, relationship dynamics, and emotional pain with patience, honesty, and mutual respect.',
	'ip_about_14' => 'Our consulting rooms and accessibility',
	'ip_about_15' => 'Our practice is located on the second floor at 18 Alder Row in the Riverside District. The rooms are deliberately understated and calm, furnished with comfortable armchairs, natural wood surfaces, and soft daylight from the windows. Ensuring our rooms are welcoming to everyone is essential to our ethos. The building provides a step-free entrance from street level and an elevator to the second floor, ensuring complete accessibility for visitors with mobility aids. A quiet waiting area with fresh water and comfortable seating is available if you arrive ahead of your scheduled time.',
	'ip_about_16' => 'Meet the practitioners',
	'ip_approach_17' => 'The way we work',
	'ip_approach_18' => 'Our approach',
	'ip_approach_19' => 'Quiet attention',
	'ip_approach_20' => 'How we think about therapy',
	'ip_approach_21' => 'We view psychotherapy as a thoughtful, collaborative process designed around the specific needs, background, and rhythm of each individual.',
	'ip_approach_22' => 'What we believe',
	'ip_approach_23' => 'Distress is not a flaw|in who you are.',
	'ip_approach_24' => 'It is a sign of something carried|for too long.',
	'ip_approach_25' => 'We listen first,|and the rest follows slowly.',
	'ip_approach_26' => 'What we believe about healing and change',
	'ip_approach_27' => 'We believe psychological distress is not a personal failure, weakness, or flaw to be mechanically corrected. Anxiety, grief, and emotional exhaustion are often completely natural responses to prolonged professional strain, painful relationship ruptures, profound bereavement, or major life changes. Because every person arrives with a unique history and personal temperament, we do not adhere to rigid formulas or predetermined clinical scripts. Meaningful, lasting healing occurs when you are offered sufficient safety, time, and dedicated attention to explore your inner experiences without fear of criticism. We accompany you at your own pace, helping you untangle difficult emotions with patience and care.',
	'ip_approach_28' => 'Therapeutic modalities explained plainly',
	'ip_approach_29' => 'Our practitioners utilize several established clinical approaches, tailoring them thoughtfully to your personal circumstances. We practice integrative psychotherapy, which combines developmental insight into past experiences with conscious awareness of current behavioral habits. For individuals troubled by recurring cycles of worry or self-criticism, CBT-informed methods help identify and gently reframe unhelpful thought patterns. Our foundation is built on person-centred counselling, where non-judgmental acceptance and empathetic listening allow you to safely examine vulnerable feelings. For couples experiencing communication breakdown or growing distance, Tomas Reyes provides structured couples therapy focused on establishing mutual safety and constructive dialogue.',
	'ip_approach_30' => 'Confidentiality and professional boundaries',
	'ip_approach_31' => 'A trusting therapeutic relationship requires absolute confidentiality. Everything shared within our consulting rooms is held in strict professional confidence. Your personal details and session records are stored securely in compliance with rigorous data privacy standards, and no information is ever disclosed to third parties without your explicit written consent. The only exceptions are strict legal requirements where there is an imminent risk of severe physical harm to yourself or another person, or statutory child protection obligations. Should such rare circumstances ever occur, your therapist will discuss the situation directly with you before taking any action.',
	'ip_approach_32' => 'If you would like to talk it through, a free 20-minute call is the place to start.',
