	'ip_contact_178' => 'Email',
	'ip_contact_179' => 'Three ways to begin your care',
	'ip_contact_180' => 'We offer three straightforward ways to reach out: you may book a first talk through our online form, send an inquiry by email, or request an online session. Hana Lindqvist, our intake coordinator, reviews all correspondence and responds within one working day. We will then coordinate a complimentary twenty-minute phone check-in call to discuss your preferences, outline practical details, and confirm an appointment time with the most suitable practitioner.',
	'ip_contact_181' => 'Location, accessibility, and opening hours',
	'ip_contact_182' => 'Our consulting rooms are located at 2F, 18 Alder Row in the Riverside District. The building provides a step-free entrance from street level and an elevator to the second floor, ensuring full accessibility. We are open Monday to Friday from 9:00 to 20:00, with extended evening appointments on Thursdays until 21:00, and Saturdays from 9:00 to 15:00. We are closed on Sundays and public holidays. Public transport connections and local street parking are within short walking distance.',
	'ip_contact_183' => 'We are not an emergency service. If you are in danger, call your local emergency number. Because Nodoka Counselling operates strictly by prior appointment, our staff cannot provide immediate medical or psychological crisis intervention. If you or someone you know is in urgent distress, facing acute thoughts of self-harm, or experiencing a mental health emergency, please immediately contact your local emergency services, regional emergency hospital, or national crisis helpline for immediate 24-hour assistance.',
	'ip_faq_137' => 'Good to know',
	'ip_faq_138' => 'Questions',
	'ip_faq_139' => 'Before you begin',
	'ip_faq_140' => 'Arranging the first meeting',
	'ip_faq_141' => 'Short, plain answers to the questions people ask before they get in touch.',
	'ip_faq_142' => 'How do I arrange a first meeting, and what is the check-in call?',
	'ip_faq_143' => 'You can arrange your first meeting by submitting an inquiry through our contact form or sending us an email. Hana Lindqvist, our intake coordinator, will reply within one working day to schedule a free twenty-minute telephone check-in call. This short call allows us to understand what you hope to address, answer your initial questions about our fees and scheduling, and pair you with the most appropriate therapist on our team before booking your fifty-minute first conversation.',
	'ip_faq_144' => 'Do I need to know what to talk about?',
	'ip_faq_145' => 'No. Many people arrive without an outline. We begin wherever you are.',
	'ip_faq_146' => 'In the room',
	'ip_faq_147' => 'Sessions and privacy',
	'ip_faq_148' => 'What happens during a session, and how what you say is kept.',
	'ip_faq_149' => 'What happens during our first conversation, and must I commit to more?',
	'ip_faq_150' => 'Your first conversation lasts fifty minutes, costs €70, and carries no obligation to continue. During this initial session, your practitioner will invite you to describe what has brought you to therapy and what you wish to change. You do not need to arrive with a formal narrative or specific goals. At the conclusion of the session, you and your therapist will decide whether continuing together feels right. You are always welcome to take time to reflect before booking further sessions.',
	'ip_faq_151' => 'Is what I say kept private?',
	'ip_faq_152' => 'Yes. We hold everything you share in strict confidence, within the limits we explain at your first conversation.',
	'ip_faq_153' => 'What are your confidentiality limits, and do you handle acute emergencies?',
	'ip_faq_154' => 'We are not an emergency service. If you are in danger, call your local emergency number. Everything discussed in therapy remains strictly confidential, with exceptions limited to situations involving imminent physical danger or mandatory legal child protection disclosures. Because we operate purely as an outpatient practice with scheduled appointments between Monday and Saturday, we cannot offer emergency crisis intervention. In an urgent mental health crisis, please reach out to hospital emergency departments or emergency crisis helplines immediately.',
	'ip_faq_155' => 'Money and time',
	'ip_faq_156' => 'Fees and cancellation',
	'ip_faq_157' => 'Fees are listed in full on the fees page.',
	'ip_faq_158' => 'What are your fees, sliding-scale arrangements, and cancellation terms?',
	'ip_faq_159' => 'Individual sessions cost €95 for 50 minutes, extended sessions are €140 for 80 minutes, and couples sessions are €160 for 80 minutes. Online sessions are €90 for 50 minutes, and a five-session individual package is available for €450. We also provide four sliding-scale places per week for individuals experiencing financial hardship. Appointments may be rescheduled or cancelled without fee up to twenty-four hours in advance; late cancellations are charged at the standard rate.',
	'ip_faq_160' => 'How soon can I be seen?',
	'ip_faq_161' => 'We reply to every enquiry within one working day, and evening slots are open on Thursdays until 21:00.',
	'ip_faq_162' => 'We are not an emergency service. If you are in danger, call your local emergency number.',
	'ip_fees_100' => '9:00–20:00',
	'ip_fees_101' => 'Saturday',
	'ip_fees_102' => '9:00–15:00',
	'ip_fees_103' => 'Sunday and public holidays',
	'ip_fees_104' => 'Closed',
	'ip_fees_105' => 'Cancellation terms and appointments',
	'ip_fees_106' => 'Because consulting hours are reserved specifically for each individual, we require advance notice if you need to alter your schedule. Appointments may be rescheduled or cancelled free of charge up to twenty-four hours prior to your scheduled start time. Cancellations made with less than twenty-four hours notice or missed appointments may be billed at the full session rate, as that dedicated time cannot be offered to other clients at short notice.',
	'ip_fees_85' => 'Practical details',
	'ip_fees_86' => 'Fees & hours',
	'ip_fees_87' => 'Plain and in advance',
	'ip_fees_88' => 'All fees in euros',
	'ip_fees_89' => 'We provide clear, straightforward fee information and regular consulting hours so you can arrange your care with complete certainty.',
	'ip_fees_90' => 'Payment and receipts',
	'ip_fees_91' => 'Sliding-scale places: four each week for people on a tight budget. A detailed receipt is given after every appointment, suitable for insurance or tax records.',
	'ip_fees_92' => 'Opening hours',
	'ip_fees_93' => 'When the rooms are open',
	'ip_fees_94' => 'Our consulting rooms are open Monday through Friday from 9:00 to 20:00, with extended evening appointments available on Thursdays until 21:00. On Saturdays, we are open from 9:00 to 15:00. We are closed on Sundays and public holidays. When you submit an inquiry through our website or send an email, Hana Lindqvist or another team member will reply within one working day. Inquiries received during weekend closures or public holidays are addressed promptly on the following working morning.',
	'ip_fees_95' => 'Monday to Wednesday',
