	'ip_first_43' => 'Getting started',
	'ip_first_44' => 'Your first conversation',
	'ip_first_45' => 'Before, during, after',
	'ip_first_46' => 'Three steps, each one yours',
	'ip_first_47' => 'We have designed the initial steps of therapy to be calm, transparent, and entirely free from obligation or pressure.',
	'ip_first_48' => 'Before your visit: the free check-in call',
	'ip_first_49' => 'Your journey begins when you get in touch by email or through our online booking form. Hana Lindqvist, our intake coordinator, will reply within one working day to arrange a complimentary twenty-minute check-in call by telephone. This conversation gives you a chance to share briefly what is bringing you to counselling, ask any practical questions about fees or schedules, and allow us to match you thoughtfully with the therapist whose experience and availability best fit your needs. There is no charge for this preliminary call.',
	'ip_first_50' => 'During and after your fifty-minute session',
	'ip_first_51' => 'Your first conversation lasts fifty minutes and carries a fee of €70. When you arrive, your therapist will invite you to speak about whatever feels most pressing, entirely at your own pace. You do not need to bring prepared notes, medical records, or formal summaries; simply arrive as you are. Following the session, you are encouraged to take time to reflect on whether the conversation felt supportive and helpful. There is no pressure or obligation to continue. If you decide to proceed, we will establish a regular schedule together.',
	'ip_first_52' => 'What the room is like',
	'ip_first_53' => 'Two chairs, a low table,|a glass of water.',
	'ip_first_54' => 'Afternoon light on a plaster wall.',
	'ip_first_55' => 'Nobody here is in a hurry.',
	'ip_first_56' => 'The consulting room and cancellation policy',
	'ip_first_57' => 'Our consulting room at 18 Alder Row is quiet and protected from street noise. Furnished with two comfortable armchairs, an oak side table with a glass of water, and warm afternoon light, it offers an unhurried atmosphere where you can speak in total privacy. If your circumstances change and you need to cancel or reschedule your first conversation, you may do so without charge provided you notify us at least twenty-four hours before your appointment time. Cancellations with less than twenty-four hours notice may be billed at the standard rate.',
	'ip_first_58' => 'The first conversation is €70 and carries no obligation to continue.',
	'ip_help_33' => 'The difficulties we work with',
	'ip_help_34' => 'What we help with',
	'ip_help_35' => 'Seven areas',
	'ip_help_36' => 'You do not need a diagnosis',
	'ip_help_37' => 'We provide individual and couples therapy across seven main areas of difficulty, offering dedicated support through times of strain and transition.',
	'ip_help_38' => 'Seven core difficulties we address',
	'ip_help_39' => 'Our practice supports individuals and couples facing seven core difficulties: anxiety and worry, low mood, grief and loss, work stress and burnout, relationships and couples, life changes, and sleep and restlessness. You might notice physical signs like persistent tension, shallow breathing, or difficulty falling asleep, as well as emotional patterns such as feeling numb, chronically overwhelmed by professional obligations, or disconnected from those you love. In our work together, we examine how these difficulties present in your daily life, identify their underlying triggers, and help you develop practical emotional resilience and clearer boundaries.',
	'ip_help_40' => 'How we work through these challenges',
	'ip_help_41' => 'Rather than applying quick fixes or generic advice, we focus on understanding the emotional context of your struggles. When addressing anxiety and disrupted sleep, we look at physiological grounding and cognitive habits. When supporting those experiencing low mood or burnout, we explore chronic workplace demands, neglected personal needs, and sustainable self-care routines. In times of bereavement or disorienting life transitions, we provide steady accompaniment through the natural stages of adjustment. Each session offers a calm, structured space to reflect, gain clarity, and foster lasting emotional well-being.',
	'ip_help_42' => 'We are not an emergency service. If you are in danger, call your local emergency number. Nodoka Counselling provides scheduled outpatient therapy and cannot offer immediate crisis intervention or emergency walk-in psychiatric assistance. If you are experiencing acute suicidal thoughts, severe impulses toward self-harm, or an acute medical or psychiatric crisis, please contact your regional emergency services, go to the nearest hospital emergency department, or call a dedicated crisis telephone helpline immediately. Our practice is designed for ongoing, structured psychotherapeutic support rather than emergency medical care.',
	'ip_online_107' => 'From your own room',
	'ip_online_108' => 'Online sessions',
	'ip_online_109' => 'Video sessions',
	'ip_online_110' => 'The same attention, on a screen',
	'ip_online_111' => 'For clients who cannot attend in person, we offer secure online psychotherapy with the exact same clinical care and attention.',
	'ip_online_112' => 'Online, 50 minutes, €90',
	'ip_online_113' => 'A familiar room,|a steady voice.',
	'ip_online_114' => 'Fifty minutes,|set aside for you.',
	'ip_online_115' => 'The same care,|wherever you sit.',
	'ip_online_116' => 'How remote consultations work',
	'ip_online_117' => 'Our online sessions provide the same attentive, confidential care as our in-person meetings at Alder Row. Conducted over a secure, professional video platform, each online session lasts fifty minutes and carries a fee of €90. Remote sessions are well suited for individuals with demanding schedules, those living outside the Riverside District, or clients who frequently travel. Lin Qiao also provides bilingual online therapy in both English and Mandarin, enabling clients to express complex emotions in their native language.',
	'ip_online_118' => 'Preparing your personal space',
	'ip_online_119' => 'To ensure a successful and reflective online session, we recommend choosing a private room where you will not be interrupted or overheard by family, roommates, or coworkers. You will need a reliable computer, laptop, or tablet with a working camera, a stable internet connection, and headphones to optimize audio clarity and protect your privacy. Setting up a comfortable armchair with a notebook and a glass of water nearby helps create a dedicated, therapeutic setting within your own home.',
	'ip_online_120' => 'Digital security and confidentiality',
	'ip_online_121' => 'We treat digital privacy with the utmost seriousness. Our video platform utilizes healthcare-grade end-to-end encryption to safeguard your data. No consultations are ever recorded, tracked, or archived. Your therapist conducts every online session from behind closed doors inside our quiet consulting rooms at 18 Alder Row, ensuring total confidentiality on our end. We ask that you similarly connect from a private, secure location rather than public spaces or shared offices.',
	'ip_online_122' => 'To meet online, write to us and tell us you would prefer a video session.',
	'ip_stories_123' => 'Composite stories',
	'ip_stories_124' => 'Stories',
	'ip_stories_125' => 'Stories of change',
	'ip_stories_126' => 'Details changed, nothing promised',
	'ip_stories_127' => 'These composite client stories are shared with permission and with all identifying details changed to illustrate how therapy unfolds. Every course is different, and these stories describe a process rather than a result.',
	'ip_stories_128' => 'The Sunday dread',
	'ip_stories_129' => 'Work stress · 12 sessions',
	'ip_stories_130' => 'A senior project manager found anxiety creeping into her Sunday afternoons, as she anticipated emails and deadlines before the week had even begun. Over twelve sessions with Samuel Okafor, she looked at how long-running pressure and perfectionism had worn on her body and her sleep. Together they explored why saying no felt so difficult, tried out boundaries she could keep, and made time again for hobbies she had set aside.',
	'ip_stories_131' => 'After the move',
	'ip_stories_132' => 'Life change and loneliness · 8 sessions',
	'ip_stories_133' => 'After relocating across continents for a new job, a young professional felt a sense of isolation he had not expected. Over eight sessions with Lin Qiao, working in both English and Mandarin, he gave words to the grief of leaving familiar communities and to the vulnerability of beginning again. They talked about how adjusting to a new culture can be tiring, and about small, realistic ways of building connection in a new city.',
	'ip_stories_134' => 'Two people, one kitchen table',
	'ip_stories_135' => 'Couples · 10 sessions',
